  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x({y}^{2}-1)}{{y}^{2}(x+3)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & x<0\\,\\text{or}\\,y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{X}(x),$ the marginal CDF of $X,$ for $x\\ge 1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=F(x,\\infty )={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }(\\frac{x({y}^{2}-1)}{{y}^{2}(x+3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x+3}{lim}_{y\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{y}^{2}-1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x+3}{lim}_{y\\to \\infty }(1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x+3}{lim}_{y\\to \\infty }(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
